#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kmplot;"
msgstr "Uso de &kmplot;"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmplot; deals with named functions, which can be specified in terms of "
"Cartesian coordinates (called <quote>explicit functions</quote>"
"), polar coordinates or as parametric functions. To enter a function, choose "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Plot</guimenu><guimenuitem>Edit Plots...</guimenuitem> "
"</menuchoice>. You can also enter new functions in the <guilabel>"
"Function equation</guilabel> text box in the main &kmplot; window. The text box "
"can handle explicit and polar functions. Each function you enter must have a "
"unique name (&ie;, a name that is not taken by any of the existing functions "
"displayed in the list box). A function name will be automatically generated if "
"you do not specify one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on &kmplot; functions, see <xref linkend=\"reference\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: using.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here is a screenshot of the &kmplot; welcome window"
msgstr "Esta é unha captura de pantalla da xanela de benvida de &kmplot;"

#. Tag: phrase
#: using.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot"
msgstr "Captura de Pantalla"

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "Function Types"
msgstr "Tipos de Función"

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:37
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Explicit Functions"
msgstr "Funcións Implícitas"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:38
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enter an explicit function (&ie;, a function in the form y=f(x)) into "
"&kmplot;, just enter it in the following form: <screen>\n"
"<userinput><replaceable>f</replaceable>(<replaceable>x</replaceable>"
")=<replaceable>expression</replaceable></userinput>\n"
"</screen> Where:"
msgstr ""
"Para introducir unha función explícita (&ie;, unha función coa forma y=f(x)), "
"simplesmente escreba-a coa seguinte forma: <screen><userinput><replaceable>"
"f</replaceable>(<replaceable>x</replaceable>) = <replaceable>"
"expresión</replaceable></userinput></screen> onde:"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:43
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<replaceable>f</replaceable> is the name of the function, and can be any string "
"of letters and numbers you like, provided it does not start with any of the "
"letters x, y or r (since these are used for parametric and polar functions)."
msgstr ""
"<replaceable>f</replaceable> é o nome da función, e pode ser calquer cadea de "
"texto e números."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:50
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<replaceable>x</replaceable> is the x-coordinate, to be used in the expression "
"following the equals sign. It is in fact a dummy variable, so you can use any "
"variable name you like, but the effect will be the same."
msgstr ""
"<replaceable>x</replaceable> é a coordenada x a ser usada na expresión do outo "
"lado do signo igual. É unha variábel parva, pode usar calquer nome para acadar "
"o mesmo efeito."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:57
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<replaceable>expression</replaceable> is the expression to be plotted, given in "
"appropriate syntax for &kmplot;. See <xref linkend=\"math-syntax\"/>."
msgstr ""
"<replaceable>expresión</replaceable> é a expresión para representar, escrita na "
"sintaxe axeitada para &kmplot;. Consulte <xref linkend=\"math-syntax\"/>."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As an example, to draw the graph of y=x<superscript>2</superscript>"
"+2x, enter the following into the functions dialog of &kmplot;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: using.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "f(x)=x^2+2x"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Parametric Functions"
msgstr "Funcións Paramétricas"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:72
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Parametric functions are those in which the x and y coordinates are defined by "
"separate functions of another variable, often called t. To enter a parametric "
"function in &kmplot;, follow the procedure as for an explicit function, but "
"prefix the name of the function describing the x-coordinate with the letter x, "
"and the function describing the y-coordinate with the letter y. As with "
"explicit functions, you may use any variable name you wish for the parameter. "
"To draw a parametric function, you must go to <guimenu>Plot</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>New Parametric Plot...</guimenuitem>. A function name will be "
"created automatic if you do not specify one."
msgstr ""
"As funcións paramétricas son aquelas nas que as coordenadas x e y están "
"definidas en funcións de outra variábel, xeralmente chamada t,  separadas. Para "
"introducir unha función paramétrica en &kmplot;, siga o mesmo procedimento que "
"para as funcións Cartesianas para cada unha das función x e y. Ao igual que "
"coas Cartesianas, pode usar calquer o nome de variábel que desexe."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As an example, suppose you want to draw a circle, which has parametric "
"equations x=sin(t), y=cos(t). In the &kmplot; functions dialog, do the "
"following: <orderedlist> <listitem><para>Open the parametric plot dialog with "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Plot</guimenu><guimenuitem>New Parametric "
"Plot...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>.</para> </listitem> <listitem><para>"
"Enter a name for the function, say, <userinput>circle</userinput>"
", in the <guilabel>Name</guilabel> box. The names of the x and y functions "
"change to match this name: the x function becomes <guilabel>"
"xcircle(t)</guilabel> and the y function becomes <guilabel>ycircle(t)</guilabel>"
".</para> </listitem> <listitem> <para>In the x and y boxes, enter the "
"appropriate equations, &ie;, <guilabel>xcircle(t)=</guilabel><userinput>"
"sin(t)</userinput> and <guilabel>ycircle(t)=</guilabel><userinput>"
"cos(t)</userinput>.</para> </listitem> </orderedlist> Click on <guibutton>"
"OK</guibutton> and the function will be drawn."
msgstr ""

