#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:144
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Entering Functions in Polar Coordinates"
msgstr "Funcións en Coordenadas Polares"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:146
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Polar coordinates represent a point by its distance from the origin (usually "
"called r), and the angle a line from the origin to the point makes with the "
"x-axis (usually represented by the Greek letter theta). To enter functions in "
"polar coordinates, use the menu entry <menuchoice><guimenu>Plot</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>New Polar Plot...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>"
". In the box labeled <guilabel>r</guilabel>, complete the function definition, "
"including the name of the theta variable you want to use, &eg;, to draw the "
"Archimedes' spiral r=theta, enter: <screen>\n"
"<userinput>\n"
"(theta)=theta\n"
"</userinput>\n"
"</screen> so that the whole line reads <quote>r(theta)=theta</quote>"
". Note that you can use any name for the theta variable, so <quote>"
"r(foo)=foo</quote> would have produced exactly the same output."
msgstr ""
"As coordenadas polares representan un ponto mediante a sua distancia á orixe "
"(chamado polo xeral r), e o ángulo que forma co eixo x unha liña que vaia desde "
"a orixe ao ponto  (xeralmente representado pola letra grega teta: &thgr;, que "
"en galego non leva \"h\"). Para escreber funcións en coordenadas polares, cree "
"unha nova Gráfica Polar co botón <guilabel>Crear Nova Gráfica</guilabel>"
". No campo de definición, escreba a definición da función, incluindo o nome da "
"variábel teta que desexe usar, &eg;, para representar a espiral de Arquimedes r "
"= &thgr;, introduza: <screen><userinput>r(teta) = teta</userinput></screen> "
"de maneira que a liña conteña <quote>r(teta) = teta</quote>"
". Lembre que pode usar calquer nome para a variábel  teta, polo que <quote>"
"r(angulo) = angulo</quote> terá o mesmo resultado."

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "Combining Functions"
msgstr "Composición de Funcións"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Functions can be combined to produce new ones. Simply enter the functions after "
"the equals sign in an expression as if the functions were variables. For "
"example, if you have defined functions f(x) and g(x), you can plot the sum of f "
"and g with:"
msgstr ""
"As funcións poden ser combinadas para xerar novas funcións. Simplesmente "
"escreba as funcións tras o signo igual como se as funcións fosen variábeis. Por "
"exemplo, se ten definidas as funcións f(x) e g(x), pode grafar a suma de f e g "
"mediante:"

#. Tag: screen
#: using.docbook:170
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput>\n"
"sum(x)=f(x)+g(x)\n"
"</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>suma(x) = f(x) + g(x)</userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that you can only combine functions of the same type, &eg; an explicit "
"function cannot be combined with a polar function."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the appearance of functions"
msgstr "Mudando a aparencia das funcións"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:179
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the appearance of a function's graph on the main plot window, select "
"the function in the <guilabel>Edit Plots</guilabel> dialog, and click on the "
"<guibutton>Edit</guibutton> button. In the dialog which appears, you can change "
"the line width in the text box, and the color of the function's graph by "
"clicking on the color button at the bottom. If you are editing an explicit "
"function, you will see a dialog with three tabs. In the first one you specify "
"the equation of the function. The <guilabel>Derivatives</guilabel> "
"tab lets you draw the first and second derivative to the function. With the "
"<guilabel>Integral</guilabel> tab you can draw the integral of the function "
"which is calculated using Euler's method."
msgstr ""
"Se está a editar unha función Cartesiana, o editor de funcións terá tres "
"páxinas. Na primeira especifícase a ecuación da función. A pestana <guilabel>"
"Derivadas</guilabel> permite-lle representar a primeira e a segunda derivada da "
"función. Na pestana <guilabel>Integral</guilabel> pode representar a integral "
"da función."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another way to edit a function is to right click on the graph. In the popup "
"menu that appears, choose <guibutton>Edit</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on the popup menu, see <xref linkend=\"popupmenu\"/>."
msgstr ""

